      "rev_n_8_b3c720_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_8_b3c720_0",
        "node_id": "n_8_b3c720",
        "thought_text": "Another approach could involve sorting the targets based on their frequency in rows and columns, then iterating through them to find the optimal placement of the bomb that maximizes the destruction of targets. This would require checking each target to see if placing the bomb on its row or column results in the destruction of the most targets.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-842408006498346188",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794404223.736604
      },
      "rev_n_9_e509b8_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_9_e509b8_0",
        "node_id": "n_9_e509b8",
        "thought_text": "A third strategy could be to use a greedy algorithm where we prioritize placing the bomb on the row or column with the highest number of targets. After placing the bomb, we remove the affected targets from consideration and repeat the process until no more targets remain. This approach ensures that we always make the locally optimal choice at each step.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-842408006498346188",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794404223.7366312
      },
      "rev_n_10_bee79a_0": {
